(vector (map (:adr/authoritative_for (vector "kotoba-lang/io-libp2p の実TCPトランスポート（kotoba.net.transport.tcp）の設計根拠" "「kotoba-lang/net」旧称と kotoba-lang/io-libp2p 正式名の対応関係の記録")), (:adr/supersedes (vector)), (:adr/superseded_by (vector)), (:adr/topic "telecom-independent-substrate-dtn-rcs-mesh-satellite"), (:adr/related (vector "90-docs/adr/2607162033-kotoba-lang-wire-shared-transport-dtn-refactor.edn" "90-docs/adr/2607162110-kotoba-lang-turn-real-udp-relay-listener.edn" "orgs/kotoba-lang/io-libp2p" "orgs/kotoba-lang/wire")), (:adr/status :accepted), (:adr/id "adr-2607162135-kotoba-lang-io-libp2p-real-tcp-transport"), (:adr/doc_type :adr), (:adr/last_verified "2026-07-16"), (:adr/body "---\nid: adr-2607162135-kotoba-lang-io-libp2p-real-tcp-transport\ntitle: \"ADR-2607162135: kotoba-lang/io-libp2p gains a real TCP gossip/bitswap transport (Phase 4), built on kotoba-lang/wire\"\nstatus: accepted\ndoc_type: adr\ntopic: telecom-independent-substrate-dtn-rcs-mesh-satellite\nauthoritative: true\nlast_verified: 2026-07-16\nauthoritative_for:\n  - kotoba-lang/io-libp2p の実TCPトランスポート（kotoba.net.transport.tcp）の設計根拠\n  - 「kotoba-lang/net」旧称と kotoba-lang/io-libp2p 正式名の対応関係の記録\nrelated:\n  - 90-docs/adr/2607162033-kotoba-lang-wire-shared-transport-dtn-refactor.edn\n  - 90-docs/adr/2607162110-kotoba-lang-turn-real-udp-relay-listener.edn\n  - orgs/kotoba-lang/io-libp2p\n  - orgs/kotoba-lang/wire\nsupersedes: []\nsuperseded_by: []\n---\n\n# ADR-2607162135: kotoba-lang/io-libp2p gains a real TCP gossip/bitswap transport (Phase 4), built on kotoba-lang/wire\n\n**Status**: accepted\n**Date**: 2026-07-16\n**Deciders**: Jun Kawasaki\n\n## Problem\n\nThis is Phase 4 of the net/turn/dtn shared-lib consolidation, the second\nof two \"give the protocol-semantics-only library real I/O\" phases\n(Phase 3a/3b did this for TURN). The repo referred to throughout this ADR\nseries' earlier documents as `kotoba-lang/net` — pure `.cljc` gossip\nfanout/dedup (`kotoba.net.gossip`) and bitswap want/have + delta-sync\n(`kotoba.net.bitswap`) semantics, explicitly \"no real network I/O ... left\nto a future native adapter\" per its own README — needed that adapter\nbuilt, sharing `kotoba-lang/wire`'s transport plumbing rather than\nreinventing it, the same dependency-efficiency demonstrated for\n`kotoba-lang/dtn` (Phase 2) and `kotoba-lang/org-ietf-turn` (Phase 3b).\n\n## Decision\n\n### Decision 0 (recorded before the substantive work): `kotoba-lang/net` is a GitHub redirect alias; the canonical name is `kotoba-lang/io-libp2p`\n\nWhile registering this phase's pin advance in the manifest, `gh api\nrepos/kotoba-lang/net` resolved to `full_name: \"kotoba-lang/io-libp2p\"` —\nthe same rename pattern this series already found for\n`kotoba-lang/turn` → `kotoba-lang/org-ietf-turn` (ADR-2607161956\nDecision 3). `manifest/repos.edn` already had the correct mapping recorded\nin its `:path-overrides` (`\"orgs/kotoba-lang/net\" → \"orgs/kotoba-lang/io-libp2p\"`),\nand `io-libp2p` was already a registered west project — this ADR's own\nmanifest change is a plain 1-line pin advance on the EXISTING `io-libp2p`\nentry, not a new registration (an initial attempt to add\n`orgs/kotoba-lang/net` as a fresh `:extra-projects` entry was made and then\nreverted once the override was found, to avoid a redundant/confusing\nduplicate path in the policy file). The implementing agent's own work used\nthe `kotoba-lang/net` alias throughout (clone/push both worked via GitHub's\nredirect, same as the `turn` alias did in Phase 1) — harmless for the\nactual git operations, but future references in this ADR series should say\n`kotoba-lang/io-libp2p`. This ADR's title and body use the canonical name\nthroughout despite the source material (the agent's own commit messages,\nits prior README) still saying \"net\" in places — a naming-hygiene follow-up\n(updating in-repo self-references to the canonical name) is additive,\noptional future work, not required to land this ADR.\n\n### Decision 1: `kotoba.net.transport.tcp` — real gossip fanout and bitswap request/response, entirely on `kotoba-lang/wire`\n\n`start-node!`/`stop-node!`/`publish!`/`want!`/`request-commits-since!`,\ndispatching inbound frames on an explicit `:kind` envelope tag\n(`:gossip`/`:bitswap-want`/`:bitswap-commits-since`) decoded via\n`kotoba.wire.edn`, delivered via `kotoba.wire.tcp`'s `start-server!`/\n`connect-or-reuse!`/`send-framed!` — the exact same API `kotoba-lang/dtn`'s\ntransport already consumes (Decision confirmed by direct reuse, not\nindependent reimplementation). `kotoba.net.gossip`/`kotoba.net.bitswap`'s\nexisting pure semantics and API were not modified — this ADR is a pure\nconsumer of them, matching the \"wrap a pure domain-computation library,\ndon't reimplement its algorithm inline\" pattern this workspace already\nestablished for `kotoba-lang/apn` (ADR-2607084700).\n\nFor bitswap, the local \"what content do I have\" (`:have-set`) and \"what's\nmy commit history\" (`:commit-log`) are accepted as `start-node!` options\nrather than owned by the transport — correctly treating \"what content\nexists locally\" as a host/application concern the transport layer has no\nbusiness deciding, the same \"host injects every concrete capability\"\ndiscipline `koe`'s dialog loop and `kotoba.dtn.dtn.gateway`'s structural\ndecoupling both already use.\n\n### Decision 2: two real friction points found in `gossip.cljc`, worked around at the transport layer without modifying the pure library\n\n1. `content-hash`'s ClojureScript branch requires `goog.crypt.Sha256`,\n   which `nbb` doesn't bundle (only `shadow-cljs`-built browser/Node\n   targets provide it). A local `src/goog/crypt/Sha256.cljs` shim, backed\n   by Node's `node:crypto` core module (verified against real SHA-256 test\n   vectors), fills this gap for nbb specifically — the same\n   no-npm-dependency discipline every repo in this consolidation series has\n   followed.\n2. `route-message`/`gossip-fanout` build an exclude set as literal\n   `#{from self}` — which throws `Duplicate key` (confirmed genuine\n   Clojure/ClojureScript/SCI set-literal behavior, not an nbb quirk)\n   whenever `:from` equals `:self`, exactly the shape a locally-originated\n   `publish!` naturally produces (a node publishing its own message has\n   `:from` = its own id = `:self`). Worked around via a `safe-from` helper\n   in the transport layer that substitutes `nil` for `:from` when it would\n   equal `:self` (`nil` is never a real peer-id, so the exclude set stays\n   correct) — per this task's explicit instruction not to modify\n   `gossip.cljc`'s existing pure API, this is recorded as a real, findable\n   bug in `kotoba-lang/net`/`io-libp2p` itself, not silently absorbed by a\n   workaround that hides it. A follow-up ADR fixing `gossip.cljc` directly\n   (e.g. building the exclude set via `(disj #{from} self)`-shaped logic\n   instead of a literal set) is legitimate, separable future work.\n\n### Decision 3: verified with real multi-process gossip fanout, including a negative control proving the dedup assertion isn't vacuous\n\nDemo scenario 1 spawns two of three gossip nodes as genuine separate `nbb`\nOS processes in a mesh topology (each node aware of the others), publishes\nfrom the third (in-process) node, and confirms each spawned process\nreceives the message exactly once — despite the mesh topology creating a\ngenuine redundant re-forward path between the two spawned nodes. The\nimplementing agent additionally ran a **negative control**: temporarily\ndisabling the seen-cache dedup gate flipped the assertion to a real\nobserved FAILURE (count=2), confirming the \"exactly once\" assertion\nactually exercises `route-message`'s dedup logic rather than passing\nvacuously for an unrelated reason. This workspace does not commonly see\ndemos include their own negative controls; recorded here as a concrete\npositive practice worth naming, not just noting the demo passed.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `clojure -M:test` → 12 tests / 53 assertions (baseline 8/40, +4 tests/+13 assertions for the new pure `kotoba.net.transport.envelope` helpers), 0 failures. `clojure -M:lint` → 0 errors, 1 warning — a **pre-existing**, unrelated `clojure.string` unused-require in `gossip.cljc` (not introduced by this ADR; independently confirmed present both before and after this ADR's changes). Independently re-run from a cold clone — identical results.\n- `nbb --classpath \"src:test:../wire/src:../bytes/src\" test/kotoba/net/transport/tcp_demo.cljs` → `RESULT: 3/3 scenarios passed`, exit 0. Scenario 1: real 3-node mesh gossip fanout with genuine dedup (negative-control-verified, see Decision 3). Scenario 2: real `:bitswap-want`→`:bitswap-have` round-trip over TCP matching the pure `bitswap/respond-to-want` output exactly, including correct exclusion of an unavailable CID. Scenario 3: real `:bitswap-commits-since`→`:bitswap-commits` delta-sync round-trip matching pure `bitswap/commits-since` exactly. Independently re-run from a cold clone by the orchestrating session — output identical to the implementing agent's report.\n- Pushed to `github.com/kotoba-lang/io-libp2p` (public; still resolvable via the `kotoba-lang/net` GitHub redirect), commit `b87f2605737d6234d8fbe2657cba6375e0fe5f48`.\n- `manifest/west.yml`: pin advanced on the pre-existing `io-libp2p` entry via `--entry io-libp2p` (1-line diff, `863284b926a3→b87f2605737d`, `verify-west-pins: 1 件の pin 変更をすべて検証 OK`); `manifest/repos.edn` unchanged (an initial incorrect `:extra-projects` addition was made and reverted per Decision 0, since the canonical entry already existed). Landed via an isolated sibling-path worktree + GitHub API server-side merge, matching every prior ADR in this series.\n\n## Consequences\n\n- Both halves of the net/turn shared-lib consolidation plan's \"give the\n  protocol-semantics libraries real I/O\" goal are now closed:\n  `kotoba-lang/org-ietf-turn` relays real UDP traffic (Phase 3b),\n  `kotoba-lang/io-libp2p` delivers real gossip/bitswap traffic over real\n  TCP (this ADR) — both built on the same `kotoba-lang/wire` foundation\n  `kotoba-lang/dtn`'s own transport already uses, demonstrating the\n  dependency-efficiency goal at three independent full-service consumers\n  now, not merely shared utility functions.\n- A real, previously-undiscovered bug in `kotoba.net.gossip` (the\n  `#{from self}` duplicate-key crash on self-originated publishes) is now\n  known and documented, with a working transport-layer mitigation in\n  place — but the pure library itself still carries the defect until a\n  follow-up fixes it directly (Decision 2).\n- The `kotoba-lang/net` → `kotoba-lang/io-libp2p` naming discovery\n  (Decision 0) means any FUTURE work in this ADR series referencing this\n  repo should use the canonical name — this ADR is the second time this\n  series has hit exactly this pattern (after `turn`/`org-ietf-turn`),\n  suggesting it may be worth a repo-wide sweep for other stale `kotoba-lang/*`\n  aliases at some point, though that sweep is not performed here.\n- Phase 5 (the originally-motivating gap: wiring `kotoba-lang/dtn` to\n  actually use `kotoba-lang/io-libp2p` for gossip-based peer/route\n  discovery and/or `kotoba-lang/org-ietf-turn` for NAT traversal) remains\n  the one phase of this plan not yet started.\n\n## Alternatives considered\n\n- **Fixing the `#{from self}` bug directly in `gossip.cljc` as part of this\n  ADR**, rather than working around it in the transport layer. Rejected\n  for this pass per this task's explicit scope boundary (don't modify\n  `gossip.cljc`'s existing pure API while building its first real\n  consumer) — but recorded plainly as a real bug with a clear fix shape\n  for a focused follow-up, not silently left undiscoverable behind a\n  transport-layer patch.\n- **Adding `goog.crypt.Sha256` as an actual npm dependency** instead of a\n  local `node:crypto`-backed shim. Rejected: every repo in this\n  consolidation series has stayed npm-dependency-free; a small,\n  test-vector-verified shim preserves that without pulling in Google\n  Closure Library's implementation.\n- **Registering `orgs/kotoba-lang/net` as a fresh, separate\n  `:extra-projects` entry** instead of recognizing it as the same repo as\n  the already-registered `io-libp2p`. Rejected once discovered (see\n  Decision 0) — would have created a confusing duplicate path for a single\n  underlying repository.\n\n## References\n\n- `90-docs/adr/2607162033-kotoba-lang-wire-shared-transport-dtn-refactor.edn`\n- `90-docs/adr/2607162110-kotoba-lang-turn-real-udp-relay-listener.edn`\n- `orgs/kotoba-lang/io-libp2p/README.edn` — https://github.com/kotoba-lang/io-libp2p\n- `orgs/kotoba-lang/io-libp2p/src/kotoba/net/transport/tcp.cljs`\n- `orgs/kotoba-lang/io-libp2p/src/kotoba/net/gossip.cljc` (the `#{from self}` bug site, Decision 2)\n"), (:adr/artifacts "{:kotoba-lang-io-libp2p \"kotoba-lang/io-libp2p @ b87f2605737d (pushed, public)\", :manifest \"orgs/kotoba-lang/io-libp2p pin advanced via --entry io-libp2p, pin-verified\"}"), (:db/id -1), (:adr/authoritative true), (:adr/title "ADR-2607162135: kotoba-lang/io-libp2p gains a real TCP gossip/bitswap transport (Phase 4), built on kotoba-lang/wire"), (:adr/source-format "edn")))